.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL = Element>
.br
class csmp::CVFEM_MathOperatorLHS< dim, CELL >"\fBBase\fP class for CVFEM Math Operators (LHS) that enable the use for control volume calculations as a post-processing step\&.

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
Philipp Weis, ETH Zuerich 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Contact"
.PP
philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch

.PP
@changes changes Latest Changes
.SH "Motivation"
.PP
In the development for the CVFEM scheme, we tested the consistency of the pressure equation and mass advection\&.
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Can be used within the CVFEM scheme (Weis et al\&., Geofluids, 2014)\&. PDE Operators that use these Math Operators as base classes can be used with the \fBCVFEM_Visitor\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
Usage and functionality as the MathOperatorLHS with the addition of access functions that are used by the CVFEM_Visitor\&.
.fi
.PP
.SH "Dependencies"
.PP
.SH "Known issues"
.PP
This construct is redundant if CVFEM_Visitors are not used\&.
.SH "Testing"
.PP
testing was done in the period before publication in 2014\&. 
